  "created": "2018-09-22T02:49:32.797Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When disabling shaders on users with the new safety system, should the default shader not be flat lit toon set to cutout rather than the Unity 'Standard' shader?\n\nGenerally this would work for most avatars as it is so highly used, especially compared to the standard shader which generally makes avatars appear dark and slightly reflective, as well as lacks cutout.",
